{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for report in core8.fix.report.md core8.fix2.report.md core8.fix3.report.md data-final.fix.report.md data-final.fix2.report.md; do git show \"bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/$report\"; done'","aggregated_output":"<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. The agent was then resumed for the data agent follow-ups; its work is committed after that report. -->\n\n## Chart core, eighth pass (controller side): report\n\n**For routing first: nothing here blocks your other two agents, but each has one request below.**\n- **Interaction agent:** add `readoutMode: 'floating' | 'strip' | 'none'` to `ControlsState` in `dom/interaction.ts`. The controller already sends it (through a cast). `'none'` means no floating tooltip and no strip; `readout: boolean` still comes as `readoutMode === 'strip'`.\n- **Data agent:** two requests, listed under \"What I need from the other agents\".\n\nNothing is committed, the tree compiles, and I did not swap the shared bundle. The new tests are in `packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts`; each reviewer sequence failed before its fix unless the table says otherwise.\n\n### Findings\n| # | Status | What changed | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Fixed, one exception | **Author code before the first write:** tick labels are made, and their AX160s collected, before anything is written (`core/axes.ts`: labels are made once per view and options, so the layout computed after the first write reuses them). Reader rebuilds caused only by labels being hidden reuse the summary already written. **In-flight pin:** the frame being published keeps its rows until it is on screen. **Callbacks:** hover, select, zoom and diagnostics raised during a frame are queued and delivered after publication. **Stale frames:** a superseded or destroyed frame never publishes an error state. **Destroy:** nothing is shown after `destroy()`. **Exception:** the interaction layer still formats tooltip and value text with author formatters during its commit. That is now safe (pinned rows, deferred callbacks) but not moved; doing so needs the interaction layer. | tick formatter appending during the frame (row kept); all formatter calls before the first host write; a commit that updates then throws (no AX199 on the newer state); destroy from a hover during commit (passes on old code too, kept as a guard) |\n| 2 | Fixed | The displayed, pending, in-flight and held frames each take their own copy of their rows once the store holds more than twice what was on screen plus 8 rows, so none of them pins history. The retention baseline moves only when the data on screen changes. | both sequences: 502 rows before, now at most 12 |\n| 3 | Fixed | A successful running append supersedes a revision held by a Resume that failed. | the full sequence: 4 stays on screen with its row |\n| 4 | Partly | New property test against an independent model, 300 runs. **Covered:** appends with and without `keep`, replacement, re-encoding, real zoom windows, pause and resume, a formatter calling back into the chart, resize to zero and back, failures at 7 stages, destroy at the end. **Checks:** drawn window against the model, caption, path vertex count, row provenance, a retention bound with no slack for extra revisions. **Not covered:** several series and kinds, re-entry from event handlers. | final-review property |\n| 5a, finding 6 | Partly | While paused, the held window's findings count for strict: a held ninth series makes `update({ strict: true })` throw. **Not done** (see the data request for the first): re-encoding keeps rows with null y on scatter; a Resume from an AX103 handler during re-encoding; an AX101 that survives a paused append. | yes |\n| 5b, finding 7 | Fixed | A call that fails while being prepared keeps what it found, then AX199, the same as `validate()`. Under `strict` this is a rejection, made before the chart changes. | four kinds compared with `validate()`; a strict create throws; a strict update keeps the last good chart |\n| 5c, finding 11 | Fixed | Tick AX160s belong to the view's tick labels, so a cached or reused layout reports them too. | loading and back at the same size: AX160 and the note remain |\n| 5d, finding 12 | Fixed | Dates in options are copied on acceptance. Zoom endpoints are copied. An instant between milliseconds, or a date or wall position that is not exact, is emitted as a number. | Date mutation in a domain; zoom Date mutation; a sub-millisecond window round-trips to another chart |\n| 5e, finding 13 | Zoom done | `zoom()` on a compact chart reports AX150 and keeps nothing, so turning compact off applies no window. The tick-format half is the data agent's. | line, area, bar |\n| 5f, finding 14 | Fixed, partly tested | `watch()` registers each watcher's release as soon as it succeeds. `theme/watch.ts` is exception-safe. Reattachment clears the document's font measurement cache (`noteFontLoad`). | `observe()` throwing leaves no media listener. Reattachment is not tested: it needs the browser, and `test/browser/chart` is the interaction agent's. |\n| 5g, finding 8 (my half) | Fixed | The hover payload is only built when someone listens. A scatter point's value is found by binary search on x, then its row among points at that x, with no walk over the series. | the existing hover tests |\n| 6, finding 9 and revision 3 rule 5 | Fixed | The mode is decided from the plot laid out without a strip. The strip height is two text line heights until measured, then the measured height. Below 240 × 140: `'strip'`, or `'none'` when the strip would leave the plot under 80 px; never `'floating'` below the limit. | 330 × 205 gives `'none'`; a plot under 140 px that keeps 80 px gives `'strip'`; a large plot gives `'floating'` |\n| 7, finding 15 | Fixed | Scatter's automatic number x domain ends at drawn ticks (`core/axes.ts`). Line x is unchanged: 1.1 to 8.9 spans its data. | both statements |\n| 8, benchmark hooks | Done | `describe()` now also gives `series[i].breaks`, `series[i].isolatedMarkers`, `series[i].keptBasis` (`'window'` for streaming charts), and `plot {x, y, width, height}`. New `memory()` returns `{bytes, buffers: [{name, bytes}]}`: `store.ownedBytes()` when there is a store, else the normalized frame, plus the scene's typed arrays, without the caller's columns. | runs and memory |\n| 9, harness resize | Fixed | `describe()` was the wrong side. In short tiles the layout widens the automatic y domain to end at ticks a short plot can draw (F7), so the drawn y mapping was right and `describe()` reported the view's narrower domain. It now reports the drawn projection's domains. | a short wide tile: the drawn domain differs from the view's, and `describe()` gives the drawn one |\n\n### What I need from the other agents\n- **Interaction agent:**\n  - The `readoutMode` field above.\n  - Author value formatters still run during its commit (tooltip and value text). To finish finding 1 completely, that text would need preparing before the frame writes. With the pins it is now safe, so this is optional.\n- **Data agent:**\n  - `data/options.ts`: report AX150 (field `y[i].tickFormat`) for every supplied tick format a compact chart cannot show, including `y[1].tickFormat` in wide form, as `x.tickFormat` and `y[0].tickFormat` already are.\n  - Finding 6, scatter re-encoding: the controller cannot copy a point frame's rows with null y, because `PointSeries.missingX` has no row indexes. It needs either a `missingRow?: Int32Array` beside `missingX` (a contract change), or a store method that returns a revision's source rows.\n- **You (`public.ts`):** on `Point` and the zoom event, a sentence such as: \"A position that a Date or a string cannot hold exactly (between milliseconds, or between days) is given as a number, which `zoom()` reads as the same position.\"\n\n### Edits outside `src/core`\n- `src/theme/watch.ts` (exception safety).\n- New `test/core/final-review.test.ts`; `test/core/host.ts` gained an `onCommit` option.\n- `test/core/controller.test.ts`: one expectation now includes `describe()`'s new `plot: null`.\n\n### Runs (last lines, final build)\n- **Type check:** exit 0. Two intermediate runs failed on `src/dom/interaction.ts` while the interaction agent was editing it; the final run was clean.\n- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 1 failed | 47 passed (48)`, `Tests 2 failed | 836 passed (838)`. Both failures are the data agent's, in `data/streaming-storage.test.ts`: the kept memory test, and \"reports owned bytes that match the retained buffers\", which is theirs in progress.\n- **Node acceptance:** `Test Files 16 passed (16)`, `Tests 512 passed (512)`.\n- **Build:** succeeded (exit 0).\n- **`packages/axylo/test/browser`, SVG:** `Test Files 4 failed | 29 passed | 1 skipped (34)`, `Tests 8 failed | 826 passed | 1 skipped (835)`. I believe none are mine; my changes only add a field to the controls state and change event timing.\n  - A8 axe, 5 kinds: \"a series hidden: label-title-only (#axylo-1-proxy)\", in the proxy's labelling (interaction layer).\n  - A5 scatter point shapes and T-tooltip-scatter (`'' to contain 'EU'`): tooltip and scatter, interaction or lookup side.\n  - `review2` \"in a card that clips its content…\": the interaction layer's tooltip placement, in their directory.\n\nLogs are `t2-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core, eighth pass: follow-up on the data agent's items\n\nAll six items are settled. Whole browser suite on SVG: 849 of 851 tests pass, 1 skipped; the one failure is in the interaction layer, not mine. Nothing is committed, the tree compiles, and I did not swap the shared bundle.\n\n### The six items\n1. **The caller's columns are now collectible.** Two new tests in `packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts` use a `WeakRef` and forced garbage collection; both failed before the fix and pass now.\n   - **(a) After a replacement:** `onFormatterError` is made once, outside `formatSpec`, so it no longer shares a scope with `valueFor`, which captured `resolved` and its borrowed table. The test replaces the columns and checks they are gone without a locale change.\n   - **(b) Streaming with `keep: 2`:** once the store exists, the accepted options drop `data`, and `resolved` and `source` go through the data module's `withoutTable`. This is done on both the running and the paused append paths; the paused path also commits the trimmed options to the options store. The test appends with `keep: 2` and checks the opening columns are gone.\n   - The tests trim the recording host's own history first, because the stand-in keeps every state it was given.\n2. **`memory()` uses `ownedBytes()`.** It returns `store.ownedBytes()` when there is a store. It adds the normalized frame only for a static chart, and the scene's typed arrays in both cases, leaving out the caller's columns. It gives `{ bytes, buffers: [{ name, bytes }] }`.\n3. **Finding 13, my half:** `zoom()` on a compact chart is a reported no-op, with tests for line, area and bar.\n4. **Finding 8, my half:** the hover payload is built only when someone listens, and a scatter point's value is found by binary search, with no walk over the series. There is nothing to pass for the pick budget.\n5. **AX199 message:** no core test pins the old text, so nothing changed.\n6. **T-tooltip-scatter is not mine, and passes now.**\n   - I built a private tree of HEAD (11fe6da) plus only my uncommitted core changes (`src/core/*`, `src/theme/watch.ts`; that copy also carried the interaction agent's `core/focus.ts`) and ran the acceptance test there: it passed. HEAD alone also passed.\n   - The failure came from changes elsewhere in the shared tree that were in progress at the time; on the final shared build it passes.\n\n### Runs (last lines, final build)\n- **Type check:** exit 0.\n- **Node suite without acceptance:** `Test Files 1 failed | 49 passed (50)`, `Tests 1 failed | 887 passed (888)`. The one failure is the kept memory test in `data/streaming-storage.test.ts`.\n- **Node acceptance:** `Test Files 16 passed (16)`, `Tests 512 passed (512)`.\n- **Build:** exit 0.\n- **`packages/axylo/test/browser`, SVG:** `Test Files 1 failed | 33 passed | 1 skipped (35)`, `Tests 1 failed | 849 passed | 1 skipped (851)`. The failure is `test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts` \"in a card that clips its content, a tooltip that would be cut off…\", which is tooltip placement in the interaction agent's directory.\n\nThe A8 axe, A5 scatter and T-tooltip-scatter failures from my previous report all pass in this run.\n\n### Still open from the eighth pass\n- The interaction agent still needs to add the `readoutMode` field to `ControlsState`.\n- Finding 6: re-encoding a paused scatter needs the new `PointSeries.missingRow` (now in the contract) wired into the controller's row freezing. That is not done yet.\n\nLogs are `t3-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a1d73b9f46c46814f, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Chart core: the three items left after the eighth pass\n\nFinding 6 and the property-test extension are done; finding 1's remaining exception cannot be finished yet, because the interaction layer has no text-preparation step to call. The full check on the shared tree has 2 failures, neither in my files. Nothing is committed, and I did not swap the shared bundle.\n\n### 1. Finding 6, the remaining parts\nThe reviewer's three sequences are tests in `packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts`; all three failed first and pass now.\n- **Scatter re-encoding while paused:** `freeze()` in `core/controller.ts` now also keeps the rows listed in each series' `missingRow`. Re-encoding `y` to `z` therefore keeps `{ x: 1, y: null, z: 11 }`, now as a point at `[1, 11]`. The arrival made while paused stays held until Resume.\n- **Resume from an AX103 handler during a paused re-encoding:** the held arrivals are now set before anything is delivered. A handler that resumes finds them, and nothing stays held on a running chart.\n- **AX101 after a valid held append and Resume:** Resume now re-reads the store with the fields as given, the same recovery a running append already had, so AX101 goes once the held rows supply the field.\n\n### 2. The property test\n- **What was added:** a second property in `final-review.test.ts`, run 200 times each on line, bar and scatter, with two series (long form, alternating).\n- **Re-entry from listeners:**\n  - a hover listener that calls `update` and `zoom(null)`;\n  - a zoom listener that calls `append`, which the independent model also takes in;\n  - hovers triggered while the sequence runs.\n- **Still in it:** the earlier operations (appends with and without `keep`, replacement, re-encoding, real windows, pause/resume, failures at 7 stages, resize to zero and back, destroy at the end), the model comparison of window and caption, row provenance on line and bar, and the retention bound.\n- **Not checked:** on scatter, hover provenance, because a point's source row index is not known to the test in a stream.\n\n### 3. Finding 1's exception: left as is\n- `src/dom/interaction.ts` still has no step that prepares tooltip or value text before the first write. Its only `prepare(state)` is the controls step, and the controller calls that during the arrangement, after the first write.\n- So author value formatters still run during the interaction layer's commit. That remains safe: the in-flight rows are pinned and callbacks are deferred.\n- If the interaction agent adds such a step, I will call it before the first host write.\n\n`readoutMode` is now in their `ControlsState` type, so I removed my cast. The controller sends `readoutMode: 'floating' | 'strip' | 'none'`, typed by their `ReadoutMode`.\n\n### Full check on the shared tree (after a build)\n- **Type check:** exit 0.\n- **Node suite (all of `packages/axylo/test`):** `Test Files 1 failed | 65 passed (66)`, `Tests 1 failed | 1409 passed (1410)`. The one failure is the kept memory test in `data/streaming-storage.test.ts` (data module).\n- **Build:** exit 0.\n- **`packages/axylo/test/browser`, SVG:** `Test Files 1 failed | 35 passed | 1 skipped (37)`, `Tests 1 failed | 875 passed | 1 skipped (877)`. The one failure is `test/browser/chart/review2.browser.test.ts` \"in a card that clips its content, a tooltip that would be cut off…\". That is the tooltip placement the interaction agent is rewriting, not a file of mine.\n\nLogs are `t4-*.txt` in `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-canarit--claude-spares-spare-6ClT4i/23402a37-81bb-469c-a14a-8bf7f048d066/scratchpad/core-fix/`.\n\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a5e106319fe97c022. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Report: data / lookup / scene / view / reader / diagnostics pass\n\nItems 2 to 8 are fixed. Item 1 is not: the kept P7 test still fails, at 17,069,760 B against the 16,000,000 B bound (it was 24,750,128 B). That bound cannot be met under the frame contract as written. No existing test's expected value was changed; I only added tests. Nothing committed.\n\n### Item 1: memory on the first append. Not fixed; it needs a contract change\n- **Why it cannot pass.** `XColumn.values` and `Series.y` must each be one array of N+1 doubles. The caller's buffers can't be extended; `ArrayBuffer.transfer` would detach the caller's arrays. So x and y alone need 16 × 1,000,001 = 16,000,016 B, which is already over the bound before slot, row or spare.\n- **The two options you offered:** \"copy only once the window has slid past the borrowed prefix\" doesn't help here. After one append without `keep`, the window still spans the whole prefix plus the new row, so it needs a fresh contiguous array. With contiguous columns, nothing passes the bound. Only segmented columns pass, and they need a contract change.\n- **Contract change I'd propose (not made):**\n  ```ts\n  /** Slots [0, head.length) may be the caller's typed column and are never written; tail holds the appended slots. */\n  export interface SplitColumn<T> { readonly head: T; readonly tail: T }\n  ```\n  `XColumn.values`, `Series.y`, `Series.slot` and `Series.row` would accept `T | SplitColumn<T>`. Every reader would have to handle two segments: view domains and ranges, lookup binary searches, scene builders, reader statistics and table, focus, controller events. One append would then cost about 1 MB (the slot head) plus small tails. The other route is for you to set the first-append budget at about 17/16.\n- **What I did change**, which brings it close to the 17 × N floor:\n  - Typed-column rows stay implicit: `row: null` is kept through in-order appends. An explicit index is built only once the window slides.\n  - The observed flags are dropped when every slot is observed.\n  - The spare tail when the store opens is capped at 4,096 slots. Later growth still doubles.\n  - x history and seed positions are views on the caller's own x column, so they don't pin a superseded copy.\n  - Point and donut columns open with the same small tail instead of 2×.\n\n**Retained bytes** (measured with forced collection; `ownedBytes()` agrees):\n\n| Case | Retained | Caller's columns |\n|---|---:|---|\n| One append | 17,069,760 B (x 8,032,768 + y 8,032,768 + slot 1,004,096 + 128) | — |\n| 1,000 appends, no `keep` | 17,078,832 B | — |\n| `keep: 2`, then retire | 1,488 B | collected |\n| `keep: 400,000` (smaller than the prefix) | 34,687,704 B | collected |\n| Explicit replacement, then retire | 485 B | collected |\n\nThe `keep: 400,000` case is large because:\n- the x, y and slot buffers are not compacted, since compaction only happens below a quarter of capacity;\n- the row index is 4.0 MB, which the contract requires once the window slides;\n- the x history copy is 4.0 MB;\n- the seed positions are 3.2 MB;\n- the retained row blocks are 6.4 MB, copied at the halfway point to free the caller's buffers.\n\nThese duplicate copies of x are a possible follow-up.\n\n**Scatter at 1M points:** 28.1 MB, down from 56.0 MB. It is still over P7: positions, x and y are copied and the row index is dense. Not fixed.\n\n**What pins the caller's columns is in the controller, not my modules.** I reproduced it in Node with the recording host:\n- **Replacement:** columns stay alive until a locale change. In `formatSpec` (controller.ts:925–928), the `onFormatterError` closure shares its scope with `valueFor`, which captures `resolved` and so its borrowed table. The formatters are reused across frames. Fix: create `onFormatterError` once, outside `formatSpec`.\n- **`keep: 2`:** columns stay alive even after a locale change. After an append, controller.ts:679 keeps `options: previous.options` (its `data` is the caller's columns object) and `source: previous.source` (the borrowed table). controller.ts:1756 reads `source.table` too. Fix: drop the static data and `source` once the store exists.\n\n### Item 2: bounded scatter pick. Fixed\n- **Design.** A pick first compares exact positions with a budget of (ceil(49 × dpr) + 1)² distance checks. If it runs over, it is redone on a second index in which every point is rounded to the device-pixel lattice. That index merges the points of each lattice point, keeping their count and latest source row, and is built lazily on the first fallback. This stays within the `Lookup.pick` contract.\n- **Why not lattice everywhere:** that would break three existing tests (the 24.125 px radius edge, the dense non-coincident pick at dpr 1, and 10,000 + 190,000 points in one cell). With exact-first, every existing lookup test passes unchanged.\n- **Visits** (`lastPickCandidates`), the same at 32,000 and 200,000 ring points:\n\n| dpr | Visits | Exact budget | Lattice |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 2,679 | 2,500 | 179 |\n| 2 | 10,137 | 9,801 | 336 |\n| 3 | 22,407 | 21,904 | 503 |\n\n  Before: 32,048 and 200,045. A dense random 200,000-point cluster stays on the exact path with 136–299 visits. The first fallback costs a one-time lattice build of about 20 ms at 200,000 points (Node).\n- **Tests:** ring tests (32,000 and 200,000 points at dpr 1 and 2), dense-cluster tests (dpr 1, 2, 3, exact and forced lattice), and a 1,500-run property test against a brute-force lattice oracle. Using floor instead of round, or dropping the later-row tie-break, makes them fail.\n- **API:** `scatterLookup` takes an optional `GridOptions { exactBudget }` (used by tests) and exposes `lastPickLattice`. Nothing is needed from the other agents. The event-payload half of finding 8 is still the controller's.\n\n### Item 3: cues. Fixed\n- New exported `barPattern(series, compact)` in `src/scene/bars.ts`. Full bars are unchanged. Compact bars use the same 32 combinations, with the pattern group computed as `(floor(s/8) + (s % 8 ? 1 : 0)) % 4` over none, diagonal, cross, dots.\n- Compact series 25 to 31 are unpatterned and differ from series 0 only by colour. Avoiding that needs a fourth pattern, which is a change to `RectMark.pattern` in the contract.\n- Scatter verified: colour and shape stay distinct for 64 series.\n- Test from the scene's marks: 32 distinct cues each for line, area, bar, compact line, compact area, compact bar and scatter. The old compact rule fails \"bar (compact: true)\".\n- **Interaction agent:** `seriesPattern` in `dom/interaction.ts` implements only the full rule. Compact bar swatches should use `barPattern(series, true)`.\n\n### Item 4: \"incomplete\" once. Fixed\n- **Tooltip model now:** rows are never qualified; `total` is qualified once (for example \"45 (incomplete)\").\n- `datum()` now qualifies only the component that has no value (\"No data (incomplete)\"). A present value no longer reads \"1 (incomplete)\".\n- With the current `focus.ts`, the all-series reading says it once: \"… S8 9; S9 No data; Total 45 (incomplete)\".\n- **Interaction agent:** keep building overflow rows plain, as `alignedRows` does now, not from `datum()`.\n\n### Item 5: wide-row summary. Fixed\n- A wide frame is now named by its series labels joined in the chart's locale (\"Visits and Signups\"). The chart-level range lists only the series that have values.\n- The chart-level y range is left out when those series have different units or scales; each series' own sentence keeps its unit on min, max and last.\n- Long form is unchanged: one label, unit on both ends.\n- Tests cover a shared unit, mixed units and long form.\n\n### Item 6: diagnostics wording. Fixed\n- New AX199 text (code, level and outcome unchanged): \"Axylo failed while building this chart: an error was thrown, printed above. If it comes from your code (a row getter, a callback), fix it there; otherwise it is a defect in Axylo: please report it with that error.\"\n- **Docs to update:** `apps/docs/data/diagnostics.mjs` and the generated `apps/docs/dist/diagnostics/AX199.html` still quote the old message.\n- AX143 was already correct. I added end-to-end tests:\n  - Vertical category bars get the suggestion.\n  - Horizontal category bars, category line and category area get the general advice without it.\n  - Bars on dates never get it.\n\n### Item 7: tick formats with no output. Fixed\nAX150 is now raised for:\n- on compact charts: `x.tickFormat` and every `y[i].tickFormat`;\n- on full wide charts: `y[i > 0].tickFormat` (\"The y fields share one value axis, labelled by y[0].tickFormat.\");\n- on donuts: `value.tickFormat` and `label.tickFormat` (\"Donut charts draw no axis ticks.\").\n\nI counted the shared-axis case as \"no output\". The docs can say so.\n\n### Item 8: byte count. Done\n- `ownedBytes(): OwnedBytes` on `AlignedStore`, `PointStore` and `DonutStore`. The types `OwnedBytes` and `OwnedBuffer` are exported from `src/data/index.ts`.\n- It returns `{ total, buffers: [{ name, bytes, buffers }] }`, with entries grouped by name. Each buffer is counted once at its full byte length, spare capacity included.\n- The caller's typed buffers are excluded; the store remembers them weakly, from the first table and from replacements.\n- It never reads frame getters, so calling it has no side effect. As a result, a frame's lazily copied tail snapshot is not counted.\n- Cost grows with the number of series and retained row blocks (about 4,000 blocks at 1M rows).\n- The test agrees with the measured retained bytes within 64 KiB for all three stores at 200,000 rows.\n- **Controller's author:** expose this through the benchmark hook.\n\n### Runs (last lines)\n- `npm run typecheck`: no errors.\n- Node suite:\n  ```\n  Test Files  1 failed | 65 passed (66)\n       Tests  1 failed | 1396 passed (1397)\n  ```\n  The one failure is the kept P7 test. At the start there were 7 failures: 6 in `core/final-review.test.ts` (controller work in progress, since fixed) plus this one.\n- Browser, after a fresh `npm run build`: render plus type-matrix gave 1 failed, 133 passed, 1 skipped. The failure is T-tooltip-scatter (the tooltip comes up empty). It fails the same way with the committed lookup files, so it isn't my change; it is probably the interaction layer, and I didn't chase it. The shared `dist` is now built from the current tree, including the other agents' in-progress code.\n\n### Files\nSource:\n- `src/data/`: `store-buffers.ts`, `store.ts`, `store-rows.ts`, `store-window.ts`, `store-unaligned.ts`, `options.ts`, `index.ts`, and the new `store-bytes.ts`\n- `src/lookup/`: `scatter-grid.ts`, `scatter.ts`, `aligned.ts`\n- `src/scene/bars.ts`, `src/reader/index.ts`, `src/diagnostics/registry.ts`\n\nTests, added only:\n- `test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts`\n- `test/lookup/scatter.test.ts`, `test/lookup/aligned.test.ts`\n- `test/scene/scene.test.ts`, `test/reader/index.test.ts`, `test/diagnostics/registry.test.ts`\n\nAll paths are under `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/`. Scratch files are removed.\n\n### What remains\n- P7 on the first append: needs the segmented-column contract change, or your decision on the budget.\n- The two controller pins on the caller's columns.\n- Scatter store memory at 1M points.\n- The duplicate x copies in the `keep`-smaller-than-prefix case.\n- A fourth bar pattern for compact series 25 to 31 (contract change to `RectMark.pattern`).\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a5e106319fe97c022, resumed. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Follow-ups: `missingRow`, and memory beyond the first append\n\nBoth follow-ups are done; nothing is committed. The bound and the contract are untouched. The kept P7 test is still the only Node failure.\n\n### 1. `PointSeries.missingRow`\n- **Where it is filled:**\n  - Static normalisation (`pointFrame` in `src/data/normalize.ts`), in the same loop and order as `missingX`, from `table.rowIndex`.\n  - The point store, as a `Column` beside `missingX`: appended, dropped by the same count on `keep`, shared through the same offset views, and rebuilt on replace and re-encode.\n  - `ownedBytes()` counts it as \"missing row\", plus \"frame series … missingRow\".\n- **Tests:**\n  - The streaming model test (1,000 runs per store) checks that `missingRow` is present exactly when `missingX` is, with one source row per entry.\n  - The shared-storage test checks the shared buffer and offsets, including the competing preview.\n  - The test comparing the store with one normalization of the retained rows now remaps `missingRow` the same way it remaps `row`.\n- **Re-encode by the store itself, tested:** a store holding `{x: 1, y: null, z: 11}` and an appended `{x: 3, y: null, z: 13}` keeps both rows retained. After `prepareReencode(store.resolveEncoding({x, y: 'z'}), version)` they come back as points: x `[1, 3]`, y `[11, 13]`, row `[1, 3]`. The row whose `z` is null becomes the missing one: `missingX [2]`, `missingRow [2]`.\n- **What the controller must call or read:** either of these.\n  - Let the store re-read: `store.prepareReencode(store.resolveEncoding(options, sink), version)`. It reads every retained row, missing-y rows included.\n  - Or, if it builds the paused re-encode from a frame itself, include `frame.source.rowAt(series.missingRow[i])` for each `i`, next to the drawn rows from `series.row`. When `row` is null, point `i` came from row `i`.\n\n### 2. Memory cases other than the first-append bound\n\n**What changed:**\n- **One copy of x per window.** For a wide chart over one sorted typed x column, the x history and the eviction seed now read from the store's own window buffer instead of each slicing its own copy. They re-point after every trim and after growth, so they never keep an old buffer alive. If the window ever didn't match the remaining prefix (checked at both ends), they fall back to the old copy-at-halfway rule.\n- **Compaction:** after eviction, any buffer more than 2.25 × its window is cut to the window plus an eighth. Previously the rule was 4× and cut to 2×.\n  - Why 2.25: growth doubles to 2 × (window + appended), so a window sliding by small appends stays at about 2× and is never cut and regrown in turn.\n  - A cut costs one copy of the window, paid for by the evictions that made it necessary. This rule is shared by the aligned buffers, the point and donut columns, the labels and the x history.\n- **Scatter: no index that only repeats the points.**\n  - The per-row `positions` column is dropped while no retained row lacks a y, because it is then identical to the points' x.\n  - The row index stays implicit while point i came from row i + shift. The frame gets `row: null` while the shift is 0, and an explicit index once points have left the front, as the contract requires.\n\n**Measured `ownedBytes()` at 1,000,000 rows, versus what the contract needs:**\n\n| Case | Before | Now | Contract floor |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Line, `keep: 400,000`, old revision retired | 34,687,704 B | 15,853,200 B | ≈14.8 MB |\n| Scatter, one append | 28,114,816 B | 16,065,728 B | 16,000,016 B |\n| Scatter, `keep: 400,000`, retired | 19,003,264 B | 15,219,648 B | ≈14.4 MB |\n\n- **Line, `keep: 400,000`:** x 3.6 MB, y 3.6 MB, slot 0.45 MB, row index 1.8 MB, rows kept for `rowAt` 6.4 MB. The caller's columns are collected. The floor is x, y, slot and the row index for the 400,000-slot frame (the index is needed because slot i no longer came from row i), plus the x and y values that events and the table need once the caller's columns are released.\n- **Scatter, one append:** only x and y, each 8,032,768 B. The floor is the same as line's: x and y must be contiguous arrays.\n- **Scatter, `keep: 400,000`:** x 3.6 MB, y 3.6 MB, row 1.6 MB, rows 6.4 MB. The floor is x, y and the row index, plus the kept rows' x and y.\n- **Line, `keep: 2`:** 464–1,530 B.\n\n**What remains above the floor:** the one-eighth spare in each buffer. And whenever some rows lack a y, scatter keeps its `positions` column; that is about one extra x copy.\n\n**Tests that count owned bytes:**\n- Line keeping 80,000 and 150,000 of 200,000 typed rows: the caller's columns are collected, the x history and seed hold at most 1 KiB, and the total is within the floor plus an eighth spare plus 64 KiB.\n- Scatter over typed columns: after one append there is no \"x positions\" or \"row\" entry and the frame's row is null; the total is at most 16 B per point plus the opening tail.\n- Scatter keeping 80,000: the total is within its floor plus spare plus 64 KiB. Before the old revision retires, the store holds \"rows kept for earlier frames\", and the test asserts that entry.\n- Disabling the sharing, or going back to the 4× rule, each makes these tests fail.\n\n**Test oracles I changed:** two scatter oracles assumed an explicit `row` array; they now read a null row as point i came from row i, which is what the contract says null means:\n- `checkFrame` in `test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts`\n- the normalization-agreement test in `test/data/transactions.test.ts`\n\nNo expected value changed.\n\n**Who is affected:** store frames for scatter can now have `row: null`. The lookup and the controller already handle that (`row?.[i] ?? i`).\n\n### Files\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/normalize.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/store-rows.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/store-window.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/src/data/store-bytes.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts`\n- `packages/axylo/test/data/transactions.test.ts`\n\n### Runs\n- `npm run typecheck`: no errors; only the `tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p tests/dist` line printed.\n- Node suite:\n  ```\n  Test Files  1 failed | 65 passed (66)\n       Tests  1 failed | 1403 passed (1404)\n  ```\n  The one failure is the kept P7 test: 17,069,760 B against 16,000,000 B.\n- Browser render and type-matrix, after `npm run build`:\n  ```\n  Test Files  7 passed | 1 skipped (8)\n       Tests  134 passed | 1 skipped (135)\n  ```\n  T-tooltip-scatter, which failed in my last pass with or without my lookup change, now passes. The shared `dist` is rebuilt from the current tree, other agents' work included.\n\nScratch files are removed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
