{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core-final.controller.review.md | nl -ba | sed -n '32,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"    32\t\n    33\t14. **M · Watcher setup and reattachment leave environment state behind. Ran with Node substitutes, traced browser wiring.** Make the theme observer’s `observe()` throw after its three media listeners register. All three remain registered. `chart.ts` also records its combined cleanup only after every watcher succeeds. Separately, change the font metrics while detached and reattach. The controller reruns layout, but the document measurement cache still returns the old width, **35 instead of 75** in my probe. DX5 and plan §2.2 require complete cleanup and fresh measurements. Register each cleanup as it succeeds, make the individual watcher exception-safe, and invalidate the document font cache on reattachment. [Watcher setup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:91) · [Theme subscriptions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:34) · [Measurement cache](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/environment.ts:89)\n    34\t\n    35\t15. **M · Automatic numeric x domains can end between ticks. Ran in Node.** A line with x values `1.1` and `8.9` commits `[1.1,8.9]` as both its full domain and its projection. The first and last drawn ticks are `2` and `8`. I read amended F7 as covering continuous x as well as the value axis. Choose the automatic x limits with the tick set and use those limits consistently in projection, lookup and zoom clamping. [X-domain construction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:258) · [X tick selection](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:64)\n    36\t\n    37\t16. **M · Series cues repeat earlier than F9 permits. Ran in Node.** Draw 32 compact bar series in one category. Series indexes 1 and 25 share a palette slot and pattern, as do six more pairs. The full bar chart has 32 distinct combinations. On scatter, indexes 0 and 64 share color and shape, and the scatter renderer has no dash cue. Preserve the 32 distinct bar combinations in compact mode and extend scatter’s marker cues and swatches when the current combinations run out. [Compact bar patterns](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:106) · [Series cues](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:73)\n    38\t\n    39\t## Displayed snapshots\n    40\t\n    41\tIn ordinary calls, `accepted` advances synchronously, `held` contains paused arrivals, and `drawn` supplies events until the next publication. `onScreen` pins the displayed rows or carries a frozen copy once the store retires them. An unmeasured frame clears old marks before dropping that pin. I reran the original Pause-to-Resume provenance sequence on all five kinds, and the pending-at-Pause case on line. I treated an append accepted before Pause as eligible for that pending draw. Both the paused retention failure and the re-entrant publication failure are independent of that interpretation. [Publication](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1297) · [Row ownership](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1346)\n    42\t\n    43\tThe property generator uses a single numeric line, finite increasing rows, mandatory `keep`, and at most 40 operations. Its zoom only resets to `null`. It generates replacements, but never re-encoding, destruction, formatter or event re-entry, resize, or any failure other than an injected reader fault. It compares prepared and committed views and checks hover provenance, but does not compare the actual path or caption with an independent model of the expected accepted and held windows. Its retention slack also leaves room for many excess revisions. I separately injected faults at all 14 instrumented stages and checked recovery and subsequent destroy. [Snapshot property](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/snapshot.test.ts:291)\n    44\t\n    45\t## Composition, registry and builds\n    46\t\n    47\tI loaded `08b469b` and `a518cbb` directly from Git into memory. Across 13 configurations, I compared create and append output, ordered diagnostics, scene geometry, overlays, lookup, navigation, swatches and table rows. I traced the browser slice-list and renderer wiring in source.\n    48\t\n    49\t| Kind | Composition compared with the old dispatch |\n    50\t|---|---|\n    51\t| Line, full and compact | Aligned storage, lookup and reader. Path, point, rule and band handlers cover the scene, cursor and focus. Line swatch and aligned stepping are connected. |\n    52\t| Area, full and compact | Same aligned paths, with fill, seam and edge handlers present for stacked and unstacked geometry. The swatch retains its fill and marker. |\n    53\t| Bar, full and compact | Band lookup, aligned reader, rectangles for bars and missing data, and rules for outlines and focus. Full-chart swatches use the mark patterns. |\n    54\t| Scatter | Point storage, grid lookup and scatter table, including missing observations. Single-series stepping and point swatches are connected. Both renderers supply point, rule and band handlers. |\n    55\t| Donut | Slice storage, lookup, table and summary. Arc handlers cover the ring and slice outlines, and rules cover focus. The slice list and its swatches remain wired. |\n    56\t\n    57\tI found no missing handler or reordered diagnostics caused by the split in those comparisons. The source bundle metafiles contain only the requested composition for each named chart export. `validate` reaches all pure data and view shapes, with no reader, renderer, scene or DOM modules. The shared temporal table-jump helper still goes through aligned normalization. It needs no other chart composition. [Compositions](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/kinds/index.ts:1) · [Table-jump parser](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/reader/x.ts:18)\n    58\t\n    59\tThe registry comparison matched **62 diagnostic constructions from the current registry tests**, in order, and **1,740 direct constructions across all 29 codes**. Full messages, including fix and outcome text, levels, effects, origins and row samples matched. Create and `validate()` matched for the 13 titled configurations. The exceptional mismatch is finding 7. An untitled `validate()` has only the kind for its name, while create can use a target id. [Registry](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts:167)\n    60\t\n    61\tThe `__DEV__ || (typeof __BENCH__ !== 'undefined' && __BENCH__)` guard folded out the instrumentation in the shipped production recipe. The production bundle contained neither hook, even with `globalThis.__AXYLO_BENCH__` set. I also ran development, a build defining only `__DEV__`, and benchmark builds with the runtime flag off and on. Ordinary strict rejection, diagnostic callbacks and AX199 recovery after a real throwing host renderer worked in both release and development. Hints reached callbacks in both and printed only in development. The internal Canvas switch remains reachable in both, as specified by decision 0002. [Controller guard](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:265) · [Hook attachment](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/instrument.ts:79) · [Build constants](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/build.mjs:44)\n    62\t\n    63\t## Verification\n    64\t\n    65\tNo files changed. `npm run typecheck` passed. The library-only serial run used Vitest with `--no-cache --configLoader runner --maxWorkers 1`. The sole failure was the typed handoff in finding 4.\n    66\t\n    67\t```text\n    68\tTest Files  1 failed | 62 passed (63)\n    69\t     Tests  1 failed | 1310 passed (1311)\n    70\t```\n    71\t\n    72\tA parallel run also failed the simplifier wall-time assertion, which passed serially. The repository-wide run hit a docs fixture that writes a temporary TypeScript config, which the read-only filesystem rejected. Browser rendering, native observer behavior, CSP and the full lifecycle heap trend were outside this run. The fixes above fit the fixed contracts.\n    73\t\n    74\t## Earlier findings\n    75\t\n    76\t| # | Status | Evidence |\n    77\t|---|---|---|\n    78\t| 1 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. The original summary callback aborts cleanly. Late layout and commit callbacks still break ownership. See 1. |\n    79\t| 2 | Fixed | Ran. All five kinds preserve the displayed row from Pause through Resume until the replacement draws. |\n    80\t| 3 | Fixed | Ran. Persistent primary mark and text failures hide surfaces and clear interaction. A subsequent valid update recovers. |\n    81\t| 4 | Partly | Ran. The original unpaused no-frame and failed-frame bounds hold, and a zero-size frame clears marks. Paused retention remains unbounded. See 2. |\n    82\t| 5 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. Ordinary paused re-encoding and recovery by title update work. Recovery by append can resurrect stale data. See 3 and 6. |\n    83\t| 6 | Partly | Ran. A rejected first append leaves controls alone, and held donut errors stay off screen. Strict updates and re-encoding miss held findings. See 6. |\n    84\t| 7 | Fixed | Ran. Nested diagnostic, zoom and hover delivery preserves the original subscriber sequence. |\n    85\t| 8 | Partly | Ran. A valid kept append repairs AX101 in all five kinds when running. The equivalent paused append and Resume still leave AX101. |\n    86\t| 9 | Partly | Ran unsubscribe collection and second-`matchMedia` failure. Both passed. The outer watcher sequence can still strand registrations. See 14. |\n    87\t| 10 | Fixed | Reasoned. Theme properties and scheme are scoped to each figure, and destroying a chart removes its figure. |\n    88\t| 11 | Partly | Ran. Subsequent appends reuse spare buffers and a title change avoids normalization and summary formatting. Handoff and caller-column retention remain. See 4. |\n    89\t| 12 | Partly | Ran. Edited plain options take effect and static label edits reuse the columns. Temporal aliases remain. See 12. |\n    90\t| 13 | Fixed with a new defect | Ran. The four original AX160 cases pass. A cached layout reused after loading loses its findings. See 11. |\n    91\t| 14 | Partly | Ran. Simple AX199 delivery and `undefined`-key parity work. An exception after an option finding still breaks parity and strict rejection. See 7. |\n    92\t| 15 | Fixed | Ran. The scatter percent and ratio examples end at 100 and 1. |\n    93\t| 16 | Fixed | Ran. The original scatter and continuous-bar windows follow the latest datum. Scatter also follows a latest observation with missing y. |\n    94\t| 17 | Fixed | Ran against amended §3.6. Category and donut zoom requests report AX150 and leave the view alone. |\n    95\t| 18 | Fixed | Ran. Two null bars produce two baseline missing marks. |\n    96\t| 19 | Partly | Ran. Reattachment rereads DPR, a language update reformats and retags output, and the themed callback batch draws once. The document font cache remains stale on reattachment. See 14. |\n    97\t| 20 | Partly | Ran live host accessors and the revised Node assertions. Inspected the stronger browser assertions. The late-setup test counts frame requests but does not assert cancellation or watcher cleanup. |\n    98\t\n    99\t- **Pending replacement.** Replacing data with a stream frame pending, then appending and zooming, produced one draw of the new data. The old hover still resolved until that draw.\n   100\t- **Donut and stack readouts.** The exercised donut kept its zero and null entries separate from Other and used one fractional share digit. The mixed stack reported `5 and -2 (incomplete)` and marked the table row incomplete.\n   101\t- **Compact references.** All three variants reported AX150 and excluded the reference from the domain and drawing.\n   102\t- **Diagnostic names.** An untitled chart used `sessions` from the target id. A subsequent titled update reported its new finding under that title.\n   103\t\n   104\tI would not release this controller. A frame can publish after losing its source, paused streams can retain unbounded history, and recovery from a failed Resume can restore retired data. The typed streaming handoff and both shipped download sizes also exceed their stated budgets.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:docs/02-product-spec.md | rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |'\"\\\\*\\\\*(F3|F7|F9|F12|I1|I6|DX5|DX7|P4|P7)\\\\b|AX199|AX143|AX160'\ngit show bbd7564:docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |bounded|retir|snapshot|P7'\"'\ngit ls-tree -r --name-only bbd7564 | rg '(decision.*0004|package.json\"'$|vitest|final-review|snapshot|streaming-storage)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:docs/02-product-spec.md | rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |'\"\\\\*\\\\*(F3|F7|F9|F12|I1|I6|DX5|DX7|P4|P7)\\\\b|AX199|AX143|AX160'\ngit show bbd7564:docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md | rg -n '\"'^#{1,5} |bounded|retir|snapshot|P7'\"'\ngit ls-tree -r --name-only bbd7564 | rg '(decision.*0004|package.json\"'$|vitest|final-review|snapshot|streaming-storage)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Phase 1b: Axylo product specification\n7:## 1. What Axylo is\n15:### 1.1 Why someone would choose it\n29:### 1.2 Who it is for\n35:### 1.3 Principles\n46:## 2. Scope of the first release\n48:### 2.1 Chart types\n65:### 2.2 Workflows\n76:### 2.3 Supported environments\n86:## 3. Acceptance criteria: the reader's experience\n90:### 3.1 Faithful representation\n107:### 3.2 Legibility\n111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\n120:### 3.3 Interaction\n131:### 3.4 Accessibility\n148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\n173:| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\n181:| AX160 | Warning | A custom formatter threw | The default format is used for that value |\n182:| AX199 | Error | Axylo itself failed while building the chart | Error state with a generic message; the error is passed to `onDiagnostic` and printed |\n188:### 3.6 Type matrix\n200:### 3.7 Compact variant\n214:### 3.8 What the evidence will and will not show\n218:## 4. Acceptance criteria: the developer's experience\n235:## 5. Performance budgets\n256:## 6. Decisions and the findings behind them\n281:## 7. Changes this revision rejected\n290:## 8. Decisions still open\n1:# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\n9:## 1. Public API\n13:### 1.1 Shape\n38:### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\n63:### 1.3 Fields\n90:### 1.4 Common options\n107:### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\n130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\n149:### 1.7 React adapter (not in 1.0)\n169:## 2. Architecture\n171:### 2.1 Pipeline\n187:| lookup | Nearest-x by binary search; nearest-point by a grid index (scatter) | Works on the frame within the visible range; cost bounded independently of the drawing. |\n192:### 2.2 Invalidation\n206:### 2.3 Rendering\n214:**Simplified drawing.** Per device-pixel column and per contiguous run of valid samples, the stroke covers the run's minimum and maximum (F5). One rule for when it applies: more than four visible samples per device-pixel column on average. The pass over visible samples is O(visible) on typed columns and is measured separately from drawing; the vertex count is bounded by width times the number of runs, not by width alone.\n218:### 2.4 Document structure\n241:### 2.5 Repository\n257:## 3. Milestones\n261:### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\n270:### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\n279:- `trend` renders in three engines at 720 and 340 px; scene snapshot; resize in both directions with no call from the page.\n286:### M2. Faithful data, on the line chart (ceiling: 8 days)\n298:### M3. Reading the chart (ceiling: 10 days)\n311:### M4. Accessibility, complete on the line chart (ceiling: 10 days)\n316:- Tab-order tests in collapsed, zoomed and table-open states; accessibility-tree snapshot after each key.\n324:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\n338:### M6. Updates and scale (ceiling: 10 days)\n346:- Budgets P1–P5 and P7 measured with the Phase 3 method, recalibrated once if M1's provisional values were wrong, then frozen with a written reason for each.\n350:### M7. Distribution and documentation (ceiling: 8 days)\n361:### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\n372:## 4. Test strategy\n378:| Scene snapshot | Vitest, injected text metrics | Geometry and text for each fixture and width, without a browser. |\n380:| Accessibility | axe-core, accessibility-tree snapshots, keyboard scripts, recorded rehearsal | A1–A10. |\n388:## 5. Risks\n400:## 6. What waits until after 1.0\napps/docs/vitest.config.ts\nbench/package.json\ndocs/decisions/0004-tooltip-and-focused-text.md\npackage.json\npackages/axylo/package.json\npackages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts\npackages/axylo/test/core/snapshot.test.ts\npackages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts\nresearch/harness/package.json\ntests/dist/fixtures/npm/package.json\ntests/dist/fixtures/script/package.json\ntests/dist/vitest.config.ts\nvitest.config.ts\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
