ptBasis === 'window'` for streams); the unexplained 24-chart resize mismatch (marks up to 13 px from the reported domain); library oddities from the docs author (`wp/docs.fix.report.md`: a wide-row summary uses the field key and puts the unit on the minimum only; the hidden plot control reads \"No data\" in the too-small state; AX199 wording); a size pass toward 96 and 80 KiB; the deferred P7 and scatter-pick items. Small record fixes for the palette author: `wp/palette-b.review.md` findings 1 to 6 (decision line 14 still says nobody else reviewed B).\n    49\t\n    50\tDecisions recorded: `docs/decisions/0001-plot-interaction-pattern.md` (unrehearsed), `docs/decisions/0002-mark-renderer.md` (SVG by default, from `bench/results/m1-renderer-comparison.md`).\n    51\t\n    52\tKnown open items carried forward:\n    53\t- View/scene review finding 10 (stack rebuilt over the whole frame per revision) and lookup review finding 12 (dense coincident scatter pick) are deferred to performance work.\n    54\t- Performance: about 80 ms for 100,000 points against about 12 ms for uPlot; profiles put it in normalization through the streaming store and in garbage collection. The fix pass moves static charts to the borrowed path.\n    55\t- Not started: documentation site, packed-distribution tests, size check against targets, scatter renderer measurement, a dist build for `@axylo/react` (must define `__DEV__` and keep the `use client` banner).\n    56\t- `docs/api/axylo.d.ts` is superseded by the real package and is to be deleted once the examples point at it.\n    57\t\n    58\t## Next action\n    59\t\n    60\t1. As the four running packages return: verify (type check; Node suite; all browser suites on SVG, `chart` and `a11y` on canvas; distribution; docs), commit each with targeted paths. The three fix agents share a tree: verify the whole only when all three have reported.\n    61\t2. A short Codex verification of the fixes against the two final reviews (read-only), then record every configuration on a quiet tree, Firefox and WebKit included; the matrix must be re-merged by an Anthropic model now (engines; React rows gone; DX1, DX7, DX8 amended; A3 rehearsal recorded as not done by the owner's decision) and reviewed by Codex.\n    62\t3. A size pass toward 96 and 80 KiB (currently 104.24 and 87.50).\n    63\t4. On a quiet machine with no agents: `node bench/decision.mjs plan` (software family about 3.2 h, gpu family about 2.2 h); then budgets P1 to P8.\n    64\t5. Conformance table (A9) from the acceptance evidence, stating no screen reader was run; agent rehearsal (DX12) against the docs; Phase 1 comparison rerun with Axylo included; docs follow-up for decision 0004 revision 3 and changed diagnostics wording.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Known limits that no agent can close\n    67\t\n     1\t/**\n     2\t * A recording host for driving the chart controller in Node (the method of the core review): a manual\n     3\t * animation-frame queue, and substitutes for the figure, the renderers and the interaction layer that keep\n     4\t * what they were given. Sizes come from a small model of the figure's CSS: the plot gets what the caption\n     5\t * and the controls leave of the container.\n     6\t */\n     7\timport type { Layout, PlacedText, Scene, TextStyle } from '../../src/core/contracts';\n     8\timport { createController, type ChartKind, type Controller, type Host, type Size } from '../../src/core/controller';\n     9\timport type { FigureModel } from '../../src/dom/figure';\n    10\timport type { Committed, ControlsState } from '../../src/dom/interaction';\n    11\timport { TOKEN_BINDINGS } from '../../src/theme';\n    12\t\n    13\texport interface Recording {\n    14\t  readonly host: Host;\n    15\t  readonly controller: Controller;\n    16\t  /** Runs every queued animation frame (and those they queue), at most `limit` rounds. */\n    17\t  frames(limit?: number): number;\n    18\t  readonly pending: number;\n    19\t  draws: Scene[];\n    20\t  texts: (readonly PlacedText[])[];\n    21\t  models: FigureModel[];\n    22\t  announcements: string[];\n    23\t  prepared: ControlsState[];\n    24\t  committed: Committed | null;\n    25\t  commits: number;\n    26\t  clears: number;\n    27\t  themeCalls: { keys: readonly string[]; colors: Record<string, string> }[];\n    28\t  printed: string[];\n    29\t  disposed: number;\n    30\t  /** Host writes (figure, renderer, text, interaction) made after `dispose`. */\n    31\t  writesAfterDispose: number;\n    32\t  /** The last surfaces(visible) call: false while the error revision hides marks and text. */\n    33\t  surfaces: boolean;\n    34\t  /** The container (CSS px). The plot's height is what the caption and the controls leave. */\n    35\t  container: { width: number; height: number } | null;\n    36\t  /** Height of one caption line and of the controls row in the model of the figure. */\n    37\t  readonly lineHeight: number;\n    38\t  ids: Record<string, string>;\n    39\t  readonly layout: Layout | null;\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\texport interface HostOptions {\n    43\t  readonly container?: { width: number; height: number } | null;\n    44\t  readonly console?: boolean;\n    45\t  readonly timeZone?: string;\n    46\t  readonly locale?: string;\n    47\t  readonly textWidth?: Host['measurer']['width'];\n    48\t  readonly captionLineHeight?: number;\n    49\t  /** The page's `lang` (A10); 'en' when not given. */\n    50\t  readonly pageLang?: string;\n    51\t  /** The target element's own id (an untitled chart's name in diagnostics). */\n    52\t  readonly targetId?: string;\n    53\t  /** Called inside the interaction layer's commit, as the DOM layer calls hover while it presents. */\n    54\t  readonly onCommit?: (state: Committed, controller: Controller) => void;\n    55\t}\n    56\t\n    57\texport function record(kind: ChartKind, options: Record<string, unknown>, settings: HostOptions = {}): Recording {\n    58\t  const queue = new Map<number, (time?: number) => void>();\n    59\t  /** Animation frame time: one value per batch of callbacks, as a browser gives it. */\n    60\t  let clock = 0;\n    61\t  let handles = 0;\n    62\t  const rec = {\n    63\t    draws: [] as Scene[], texts: [] as (readonly PlacedText[])[], models: [] as FigureModel[], announcements: [] as string[],\n    64\t    prepared: [] as ControlsState[], committed: null as Committed | null, commits: 0, clears: 0,\n    65\t    themeCalls: [] as { keys: readonly string[]; colors: Record<string, string> }[], printed: [] as string[], disposed: 0,\n    66\t    writesAfterDispose: 0, surfaces: true,\n    67\t    container: settings.container === undefined ? { width: 720, height: 400 } : settings.container,\n    68\t    lineHeight: settings.captionLineHeight ?? 20, ids: {} as Record<string, string>,\n    69\t  };\n    70\t  let model: FigureModel | null = null;\n    71\t  let controls: ControlsState | null = null;\n    72\t  const style: TextStyle = { font: '400 12px sans-serif', letterSpacing: 0, wordSpacing: 0, lineHeight: 15 };\n    73\t\n    74\t  /** The plot size the model figure gives: container minus caption (title, subtitle, visible summary) and controls. */\n    75\t  function plotSize(): Size | null {\n    76\t    const box = rec.container;\n    77\t    if (box === null) return null;\n    78\t    let used = 0;\n    79\t    if (model && !model.compact) {\n    80\t      if (model.title?.visible) used += rec.lineHeight;\n    81\t      if (model.subtitle) used += rec.lineHeight;\n    82\t      if (model.summaryVisible) used += 2 * rec.lineHeight;\n    83\t      if (model.note) used += rec.lineHeight;\n    84\t    }\n    85\t    if (controls && controls.interactive) {\n    86\t      // The legend and toolbar take a row; the fallback offers only the table control, which is a row too\n    87\t      // but shorter (no legend).\n    88\t      used += controls.tooSmall ? rec.lineHeight : 1.5 * rec.lineHeight;\n    89\t    }\n    90\t    return { width: box.width, height: box.height - used };\n    91\t  }\n    92\t\n    93\t  const host: Host = {\n    94\t    id: 'axylo-test',\n    95\t    targetId: settings.targetId ?? null,\n    96\t    console: settings.console === false ? null : {\n    97\t      warn: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n    98\t      info: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n    99\t      error: (...args: unknown[]) => { rec.printed.push(String(args[0])); },\n   100\t    },\n   101\t    page: {},\n   102\t    timeZone: settings.timeZone ?? 'UTC',\n   103\t    renderer: { kind: 'svg', draw: scene => { if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++; rec.draws.push(scene); } },\n   104\t    text: { render: texts => { if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++; rec.texts.push(texts); } },\n   105\t    surfaces(visible) {\n   106\t      rec.surfaces = visible;\n   107\t    },\n   108\t    figure: {\n   109\t      update(next) {\n   110\t        if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++;\n   111\t        const before = model;\n   112\t        model = next;\n   113\t        rec.models.push(next);\n   114\t        return before === null || before.summaryVisible !== next.summaryVisible || before.note !== next.note ||\n   115\t          before.title?.text !== next.title?.text || before.subtitle !== next.subtitle;\n   116\t      },\n   117\t      announce: text => { rec.announcements.push(text); },\n   118\t    },\n   119\t    interaction: {\n   120\t      prepare(state) {\n   121\t        const before = controls;\n   122\t        controls = state;\n   123\t        rec.prepared.push(state);\n   124\t        return before === null || before.tooSmall !== state.tooSmall || before.interactive !== state.interactive;\n   125\t      },\n   126\t      commit(state) {\n   127\t        if (rec.disposed) rec.writesAfterDispose++;\n   128\t        rec.committed = state;\n   129\t        rec.commits++;\n   130\t        if (state) settings.onCommit?.(state, controller);\n   131\t      },\n   132\t      clear() {\n   133\t        rec.committed = null;\n   134\t        rec.clears++;\n   135\t      },\n   136\t    },\n   137\t    measurer: { width: settings.textWidth ?? (text => text.length * 7) },\n   138\t    requestFrame(callback) {\n   139\t      const handle = ++handles;\n   140\t      queue.set(handle, callback);\n   141\t      return handle;\n   142\t    },\n   143\t    cancelFrame(handle) {\n   144\t      queue.delete(handle);\n   145\t    },\n   146\t    locale: option => typeof option === 'string' ? option : settings.locale ?? 'en-US',\n   147\t    pageLang: () => settings.pageLang ?? 'en',\n   148\t    labelText: id => Object.hasOwn(rec.ids, id) ? rec.ids[id]! : null,\n   149\t    textStyle: () => style,\n   150\t    measure: plotSize,\n   151\t    devicePixelRatio: () => 1,\n   152\t    theme(keys, colors) {\n   153\t      rec.themeCalls.push({ keys: [...keys], colors });\n   154\t      const series = keys.map((_, i) => `var(--axylo-series-color-${i + 1})`);\n   155\t      const paints = { tokens: { ...TOKEN_BINDINGS }, series };\n   156\t      return {\n   157\t        bindings: { tokens: TOKEN_BINDINGS, series },\n   158\t        theme: { scheme: 'light', forcedColors: false, moreContrast: false, paints },\n   159\t        resolved: true, backdropKnown: false,\n   160\t      };\n   161\t    },\n   162\t    dispose() {\n   163\t      rec.disposed++;\n   164\t    },\n   165\t  };\n   166\t\n   167\t  const controller = createController(kind, options, host);\n   168\t  // Accessors stay accessors: `pending` and `layout` are read when asked (review 3, finding 20).\n   169\t  return Object.defineProperties(Object.assign(rec, {\n   170\t    host, controller,\n   171\t    frames(limit = 10): number {\n   172\t      let rounds = 0;\n   173\t      while (queue.size && rounds < limit) {\n   174\t        rounds++;\n   175\t        const callbacks = [...queue.values()];\n   176\t        queue.clear();\n   177\t        clock += 16;\n   178\t        for (const cb of callbacks) cb(clock);\n   179\t      }\n   180\t      return rounds;\n   181\t    },\n   182\t  }), {\n   183\t    pending: { get: () => queue.size, enumerable: true },\n   184\t    layout: { get: () => rec.committed?.layout ?? null, enumerable: true },\n   185\t  }) as unknown as Recording;\n   186\t}\n   187\t\n   188\texport const lastModel = (r: Recording): FigureModel => r.models[r.models.length - 1]!;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
