{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git grep -n -e 'lossless' -e 'AX199' -e 're-encod' bbd7564 -- docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md packages/axylo/test/acceptance | head -50\ngit show bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core-final.controller.review.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,32p'\"","aggregated_output":"bbd7564:docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:181:The **frame** is the normalized, lossless data: typed columns, a validity bitmap, dictionary-encoded categories, source-row indexes and a revision number. It is the only source for exact values. The table, the summary, keyboard navigation, tooltips and events read the frame. The **scene** is geometry for drawing and may be simplified (F5); nothing reads values back from it. The first draft derived accessibility from the scene, and two reviewers showed that a simplified drawing cannot return the samples it dropped.\nbbd7564:packages/axylo/test/acceptance/EVIDENCE.json:178:  {\"criterion\":\"F3\",\"type\":\"line\",\"file\":\"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts\",\"title\":\"F3 line: AX199 reports a forced internal failure, draws a generic error, and clears old interaction\"},\nbbd7564:packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts:253:diagnostic('line', { code: 'AX199', level: 'error', effect: 'chart-error', name: 'reports a forced internal failure, draws a generic error, and clears old interaction', fix: /please report it/i },\n     1\t<!-- Reviewer: Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort max (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ee43-dc0a-70a3-83ed-4224a8dba1c6), read-only, cross-provider. Reviewed commit a518cbb. -->\n     2\t\n     3\t# Final review of `a518cbb`\n     4\t\n     5\t## Findings\n     6\t\n     7\t1. **B · A frame can lose its source rows while it is drawing. Ran in Node.** Draw a line at x `[0,1,2]`, then append `3` with `keep: 1`. In the tick formatter for that frame, append `4` with `keep: 1`. The first frame draws `3`, but hovering it returns `index: 3, row: null`. Layout calls the formatter after publication has started, and the nested append can retire the in-flight revision. I also reproduced a superseded frame’s failure putting a newer valid update into the AX199 error state. Destroying from a hover callback during commit retained the caller’s data after forced collection because `showing()` ran after `destroy()`. DX5 and plan §1.5 require a coherent publication and complete teardown. Pin the in-flight snapshot through publication, finish it before delivering interaction callbacks, and prevent a stale or destroyed generation from publishing state or errors. [controller.ts](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:982) · [Interaction commit](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1541)\n     8\t\n     9\t2. **B · Pause defeats `keep` with or without frame callbacks. Ran in Node.** Draw `[0,1]`, append `2` with `keep: 1`, pause before that frame, then append `3` through `503` with `keep: 1` and run no frames. The store retains **502 rows**. Drawing `2` before pausing and running a frame after every subsequent append also retains **502 rows**. The first sequence pins a pending revision that `release()` never freezes. In the second, each redraw of the same paused snapshot raises the retention baseline. Plan §1.5 and P7 require bounded retention. Give both pending and displayed snapshots independent ownership when they pin history, and reset the retention baseline only when the displayed data revision changes. [release and showing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1353)\n    10\t\n    11\t3. **B · Recovery after a failed Resume can roll the chart back to retired data. Ran in Node.** Display `2`, pause, append `3` with `keep: 1`, and inject a view failure on Resume. Remove the fault, append `4` with `keep: 1`, and draw. The chart shows `4`. A title-only update then puts `3` back on screen, and its hover returns `row: null`. The successful append leaves `held` pointing to the older revision, which `resumable()` later promotes. This breaks call order and provenance under DX5 and plan §1.5. A successful append after failed Resume must consume or supersede the held revision in the same acceptance step. [resumable](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:717) · [append acceptance](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:675)\n    12\t\n    13\t4. **B · The first append exceeds the retained-memory budget. Ran in Node with forced collection.** Open a one-million-point line over two borrowed `Float64Array` columns and append one row. The store retains **24,750,128 bytes beyond the caller’s 16,000,000 bytes**, before counting the whole chart. I also reproduced retention of the original caller column after both `keep: 2` and explicit replacement. A locale change that rebuilt the formatters made it collectible. P7 and plan §2.2 require a cheaper handoff. Keep the borrowed prefix with an appendable tail, avoid dense identity indexes for untouched rows, and free the original data and table-bearing formatter state when their snapshots retire. [Store allocation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:38) · [Formatter construction](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:925) · [Failing budget test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:88)\n    14\t\n    15\t5. **B · Both DX7 download targets are exceeded. Ran against the installed distribution fixture.** Bundle the documented npm example and then a consumer exporting everything. With CSS included as shipped, the results are **89,605 B** against **81,920 B** for line only and **106,738 B** against **98,304 B** for everything. The installed production ESM matched the in-memory rebuild byte for byte. The named kinds tree-shake, so the remaining work is to reduce the code and stylesheet reachable from each entry point and enforce the existing byte targets on the packed artifact. [Public entry points](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/index.ts:19) · [Size measurement](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs:60)\n    16\t\n    17\t6. **M · Paused data is only partly validated and re-encoded. Ran in Node.** Hold a ninth series while paused. The append reports AX130, but `update({strict: true})` succeeds, and changing the y field drops AX130. If a new-field AX103 handler calls Resume during re-encoding, the chart switches to running while the arrivals stay held. On scatter, re-encoding a paused snapshot also drops a row such as `{x: 1, y: null, z: 11}` when changing `y` to `z`, because `freeze()` only visits drawable points. A missing-field AX101 can likewise survive a valid held append and Resume. This violates I6, DX5 and §3.5. Build and validate both windows, preserve their complete source rows, and accept the pair before invoking callbacks. [Paused re-encoding](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:555) · [AX101 recovery](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:639) · [Row freezing](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:693)\n    18\t\n    19\t7. **M · Exceptional call validation disagrees with `validate()` and bypasses `strict`. Ran in Node on all five kinds.** Supply an unknown option `palete` and a row whose x or label getter throws. `validate()` returns AX150 followed by AX199. Create reports only AX199 and returns an error-state chart even with `strict: true`, although it already found a call-origin AX150. A strict update with a throwing row getter also replaces the last good display with the internal-error state. Share call preparation and exception classification, retain findings collected before failure, and apply strict rejection before changing the accepted chart. [Controller exception path](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:500) · [Static validation](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:156)\n    20\t\n    21\t8. **M · A scatter pointer move can do work proportional to the data. Ran in Node.** Pick the centre of a 20 px radius ring containing 32,000 points. The grid examines **32,048 candidates**. In a separate 50,000-point chart, picking the last row caused the controller to read **50,000 row indexes** to build the hover event, even though the lookup already knew the point’s index. The controller builds that payload even with no subscriber. This leaves plan §2.1’s bounded lookup unmet. I1 and P4 browser latency remain unmeasured. Reuse the located index for exact event values, skip unused payloads, and test a bounded nearest-point and coincidence query against adversarial point layouts. [Grid search](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:203) · [Event lookup](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1449)\n    22\t\n    23\t9. **M · Short plots silently skip the reserved readout. Ran in Node.** At a 330 × 205 recording-host container, a line commits a 283 × 92 plot with `readout: false`. A donut commits a 330 × 118 plot with the same result in a shorter container. The extra condition at 80 px selects a floating tooltip even though I1 and decision 0004 rule 5 require the strip below 140 px. Treat the strip as required space and evaluate L8 on the remaining plot, with the mode selected from geometry that excludes the strip’s own effect. That is my reading of how the two rules should interact. [Readout decision](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1193)\n    24\t\n    25\t10. **M · A tooltip corridor can keep a datum after eviction. Reasoned from the interaction path.** Rest on a bar whose tooltip is beside it, begin moving through the rule 3b corridor, then append with `keep` so that bar leaves the window. A same-epoch commit repicks the pointer and remaps some references, but keeps the old corridor and its target. The next move inside the old hull suppresses picking and restores the evicted target. This breaks I1 and decision 0004 rule 3b. Invalidate or revalidate the corridor, held tooltip and resting datum with the new snapshot and layout before allowing them to override picking. [Corridor hit test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:872) · [Interaction commit](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1541)\n    26\t\n    27\t11. **M · Cached tick layouts can lose AX160 and the reader note. Ran in Node.** Use a throwing y tick formatter, draw, set `state: 'loading'`, then clear `state` at the same measured size. The same fallback tick labels return without a formatter call, AX160, or the F12 note. The loading frame clears the diagnostic bucket while `lastLayout` keeps the fallback labels. Store findings with each cached layout and publish the findings for the layout actually used. [Layout cache and bucket](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1178)\n    28\t\n    29\t12. **M · Temporal inputs remain mutable and some emitted windows cannot round-trip. Ran in Node.** Mutate a `Date` in `x.domain` from January 1 to January 3 and resubmit the option. The domain still starts on January 1. Mutate the first `Date` passed to `zoom()` and then update a reference. The window moves without a second zoom call. On an instant axis, `[t + 0.25, t + 0.75]` emits two equal `Date` values, and passing the event to another chart resets it to its full range. Snapshot option dates, keep zoom endpoints as immutable positions, and emit a numeric position when a `Date` or string cannot encode it exactly. This restores plan §1.5 and the public event contract. [Option snapshots](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:43) · [Position conversion](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:191) · [Zoom acceptance](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:730)\n    30\t\n    31\t13. **M · Compact charts accept latent zoom and silently ignore secondary tick formats. Ran in Node on line, area and bar.** Call `zoom([1,3])` on a compact chart. It emits a zoom event for the full range, saves the requested window, and applies `[1,3]` when `compact` is later turned off. In wide mode a `y[1].tickFormat` is ignored without AX150, although `x.tickFormat` and `y[0].tickFormat` are reported. This violates §3.7 and F3. Reject compact zoom before changing state or emitting an event, and report every supplied compact tick format that has no output. [Zoom gate](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:730) · [Wide field resolution](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:237)\n    32\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
